<title>USA: Crestar Sept 30 Q3 shr falls, inc SAIF charge.</title>
<headline>Crestar Sept 30 Q3 shr falls, inc SAIF charge.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.86		    $1.18</p>
<p> Net		 36,800		   52,100</p>
<p>	   9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $3.44		    $3.51</p>
<p> Net		 149,000		  153,500</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Crestar Financial Corp</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said it recorded a one-time after tax charge of $21.5 million or $0.50 per share to recapitalize its share of the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>Crestar also received an after tax benefit in the third quarter 1996 of $10.6 million as a result of the repeal of the thift bad debt recapture rule. It partially offset this gain by taking a $5 millon charge for closing branches.</p>
</text>
